'' TKO0632 (it was TKO0660), fbc's 99 (T42): a type with 'operator cast( ) as double' AND 'as longint',
'' passed to a procedure overloaded for double and longint -- each overload reached
'' exactly, through a different cast -- is ambiguous, beside a builtin argument too.
'' tiko bound the double one in silence: a UDT argument kept the tie report quiet. A
'' one-cast type, a single procedure and a builtin argument still bind. Lines identical
'' to fbc-modern's errors. See UdtCastTie_ in symbols/checkbase.bas.
'' NOT A TIE, it turned out (2026-10-17): in a set an exact numeric cast is no match at all
'' (structpick.tiko NumCastArgPick), so neither overload is reached -- fbc's 99 is TKO0632.
'' 'Take( b )' with only the double cast binds the LONGINT overload.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/cast-overload-tie.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: cast-overload-tie.bas(31,5): error TKO0632
'' EXPECT-OUT: cast-overload-tie.bas(32,6): error TKO0632
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 2
